<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Gaurihar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1807 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Gaurihar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small chiefship of the Bundelkhand Agency, confirmed by British sanad in 1807.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gaurihar was one of the small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> holdings confirmed by British sanads in 1807, after the British established supremacy in the region following the wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It was a minor, non-salute state of a few dozen villages. Little else of its history is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After independence Gaurihar was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> with the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> states and absorbed by 1950; it lies in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chhatarpur-state">Chhatarpur</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/gaurihar-state.jpg" alt="Gaurihar State" width="320" height="243"><figcaption>Image: John George Bartholomew (1860–1920) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JaitpurKart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1807 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gaurihar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gaurihar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1878&amp;focus=gaurihar-state" aria-label="Gaurihar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6804 1247 640 512" role="